","The tunable properties of polymer-based smart materials are achieved by incorporating functional functionalizable functional groups or functional functionalities into the polymer structure. These functionalizing components can then be designed to respond to specific stimuli, such as temperature, pH, light, or other stimuli. This process can be achieved through various approaches, including chemical modification, chemical cross-linking, and chemical cross-polymeration.

