Determine the system reliability function \( R_S(t) \) for a non-repairable system with independent components, where the system's reliability structure is:
a) A serial structure  
b) A parallel structure  
c) A combination of serial and parallel structures<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The system reliability function \( R_S(t) \) is the probability that the system fails after time \( t \). For a non-resistant system, the system fails if all components fail. For a reliable system, the system survives if all components survive. Thus, the reliability function is the product of the individual component reliances.  

1. **A. Series System:**  
   In a series system, the system fails if all components fail. The reliability of the system is the product of the reliances of all components. If the components are \( R_1(t), R_2(t), R_3(t) \), and so on., the system reliability is:  
   \[
   R_S(t) = R_1(t) \times R_2(t) \times R_3(t) \times \cdots \times R_n(t)
   \]  
   where \( n \) is the number of components in the series system.  

2. **B. Parallel System:**  
   In a parallel system, the system succeeds if only only one component survives. The system fails if all components fail. The reliability of the system is the product of the failure probabilities of all components. The reliability of the system is:  
   \[
   R_S(t) = 1 - \prod_{i=1}^{n} (1 - R_i(t))
   \]  
   where \( n \) is the number of components in the parallel system.  

