K = ΔT / m_namylane = 0.402°C / 0.0802 mol/kg = 5.025 °C/mol dmol⁻¹

Now we can use the same K value for the unknown solute:

ΔT = 0.647°C
i = 1
K = 5.025 °C/mol dmmol⁻¹

m_unknown = ΔT / (i * K) = 0.647°C / (1 * 5.025 °C/mol dmol⁻¹) = 0.129 mol/kg

Now, we can find the molecular weight of the unknown solute:

moles_unknown = 0.6216 g / molecular_weight_unknown

We know m_unknown = moles_unknown / mass_CCl₄, so:

0.129 mol/kg = 0.6216 g / (120 g)

Molecular_weight_unknown = 0.6216 g / 0.129 mol/kg = 4.82 g/mol

