   - The distance the train must cover is the sum of the initial distance (150 m) and the length of the train.
   - Let the length of the train be \( x \) meters.
   - The distance covered by the train is \( 150 + x \) meters.

6. **Calculate the length of the train**:
   - Using the relative speed and time, the distance covered by the train is:
     \[
     \text{Distance} = \text{Rate} \times \text{Time}
     \]
     \[
     150 + x = 10 \times 25
     \]
     \[
     150 + x = 250
     \]
     \[
     x = 250 - 150 = 100 \text{ m}
     \]

