   y - f(a) = f'(a)(x - a)
   \]
   Rearranging the equation gives:
   \[
   y = f'(a)(x - a) + f(a)
   \]

This equation represents the line that passes through the point \( (a, f(a) \), has a slope of \( f'(a) \), and is tangent to the graph of \( f \) at this point.
