In summary, dark matter plays a crucial role in the formation and evolution of black holes in the universe. It influences the formation of galaxies, the formation of stars, and the dynamics of galaxy mergers, all of which can influence the formation and evolution of black holes. The presence of dark matter can also lead to the formation of primordial black holes.
