","The scattered particle is assumed to be a particle of mass \( m \), with initial four-momentum \( P_i = (E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_i) \) and final four-momentum \( P_f = (E_f/c, \mathbf{p}_f) \). The electron is the scattered particle in this case. The scattered particle's momentum transfer is given by the difference between the initial and final four-momenta:

