","(a) **Fraction of the intensity through the system**:  
1. **Reflection at the first surface**:  
   The fraction of intensity transmitted is \( T_1 = e^{-2\text{Re}(i_1)} \), where \( i_1 = \text{Im}(k_1) = \frac{2\pi}{c}n_1\sin^{-1}\left(\frac{n_2}{n_1}\sin\theta\right) \).  
   For normal incidence (\( \theta = 0 \)), \( T_1 = 1 \).  

2. **Reflection at the second surface**:  
   The fraction of intensity transmitted is \( T_2 = e^{-2\text{Re}(i_2)} \), where \( i_2 = \text{Im}(k_2) = \frac{2\pi}{c}n_2\sin^{-1}\left(\frac{n_3}{n_2}\sin\theta\right) \).  
   For normal incidence (\( \theta = 0 \)), \( T_2 = 1 \).  

3. **Reflection at the last surface**:  
   The fraction of intensity transmitted is \( T_3 = e^{-2\text{Re}(i_3)} \), where \( i_3 = \text{Im}(k_3) = \frac{2\pi}{c}n_3\sin^{-1}\left(\frac{n_4}{n_3}\sin\theta\right) \).  
   For normal incidence (\( \theta = 0 \)), \( T_3 = 1 \).  

