To calculate the average radiation dose to the liver, we use the formula:

\[
\text{Dose} = \frac{E}{\text{Mass}} \times 1000 \text{ mJ/kg} \rightarrow \text{mGy/g}
\]

Where:
- \( E = 0.12 \text{ J} \) (absorbed energy),
- \( \text{Mass} = 1.6 \text{ kg} \) (mass of liver tissue).

First, convert the absorbed energy to millijielectrons (mGy):

\[
\text{Dose} = \frac{0.12 \text{ J}}{1.6 \text{ kg}} \times 1000 \text{ mGy/kg} = 0.075 \text{ mGy/g}
\]

Thus, the average radiation dose to the liver is \(\boxed{0.075 \text{ mGy/g}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

