","To estimate the tensile yield strength \(\sigma_{yr}\) due to the presence of hard particles, we use the Oagger-Oottman (O.O.) equation for the effect of obstacles (e.g., hard particles) on the yield strength of a material. The O.O. equation is:

\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{2\pi G b^2}{a}
\]

where:
- \(\sigma_{yr}\) is the tensile yield strength due to the obstacles.
- \(G\) is the shear modulus of the material.
- \(b\) is the Burgers vector.
- \(a\) is the average center-to-center spacing of the obstacles.

Substituting the given values:
- \(G = 26 \times 10^9 \text{ N/m}^2\)
- \(b = 0.286 \times 10^{-9} \text{ m}\)
- \(a = 6 \times 10^{-8} \text{ m}\)

Substitute these values into the O.O. equation:

\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{2\pi \times 26 \times 10^9 \times (0.286 \times 10^{-9})^2}{6 \times 10^{-8}}
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{2\pi \times 26 \times 10^9 \times 8.21 \times 10^{-19}}{6 \times 10^{-8}}
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{5.2 \times 10^{-2}}{6 \times 10^{-8}}
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = 8.67 \times 10^{5} \text{ N/m}^2
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = 8.67 \text{ MN/m}^2
\]

Thus, the estimated tensile yield strength due to these particles is \(\boxed{8.67 \text{ MN/m}^2}\).",fluency,"# Task Description
