\[
\Gamma = \frac{\hbar}{2\tau}
\]  
where \(\hbar\) is the reduced Planck constant (\(\approx 1.054 \times 10^{-34} \, \text{J s}\)) and \(\tau\) is the lifetime.  

The width \(\Gamma\) is related to the width of the energy spectrum due(\(\Delta E\)) of the particle. The uncertainty in the energy \(\Delta E\) is related to the lifetime \(\tau\) by:  
\[
