The most precise measurements of the strong coupling constant come from the following sources:

1. Deep inelastic scattering experiments: These experiments involve scattering high-energy electrons or neutrinos off protons or neutrons. By analyzing the energy spectrum of the outgoing particles, one can extract information about the internal structure of the hadrons and the strong force between their constituents.

